10
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:50.390
Nico Flaig: Which is, basically, the builder doesn't know what the proposal will end up proposing on.

11
00:01:50.710 --> 00:02:05.149
Nico Flaig: So, to cover all cases, especially if there's, like, a PTC split view or WCAT, you basically have to provide the bid for empty, and if there's a payload also, you need to provide one for full.

12
00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:11.879
Nico Flaig: And then, also, in case of an honest proposal reorg, you would also need to supply a bid for the parent.

13
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.449
Nico Flaig: Which has, like, the payload status resolved already, so in that case, you only need one.

14
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:24.730
Nico Flaig: I previously had this to even cover at least two branches with a different head.

15
00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.369
Nico Flaig: But Portus was not so happy with that, so I removed that. I think.

16
00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.409
Nico Flaig: Having just 3 is probably enough.

17
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:44.690
Nico Flaig: I think the only… I mean, the consideration is, like, implementation complexity, but we already have the, sync… No, sorry, the…

18
00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:56.269
