43
00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:11.459
potuz: So, I want to give an argument against this change, but also, it's not really against this change, but actually against the current spec.

44
00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.040
potuz: Oh.

45
00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:21.999
potuz: The way we have our cash now is that we… we keep a highest value for a pair of

46
00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.729
potuz: Block and hash.

47
00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:32.809
potuz: And already this is bad enough that it allows builders to propagate beds

48
00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:40.010
potuz: And keep increasing the value without the fear of them being included, because if there's an overwhelming

49
00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.749
potuz: Already decision on the chain on what's the head view.

50
00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:51.050
potuz: Then they can keep increasing the bid value on the non-head blog.

51
00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:55.690
potuz: And try to bid on that, and those bits will propagate because of the cache.

52
00:06:56.150 --> 00:07:06.189
potuz: So this PR makes this strictly worse, in that a builder might just keep increasing the value and keep DOSsing the P2P stack with bids.

53
00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.800
potuz: For blocks that can never be proposed by an honest proposer.

54
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.280
potuz: And we won't stop this.

55
00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:24.359
potuz: I believe that the easiest, safe way of dealing with the P2P stack for bids would be that you propagate the best bid that you have seen

56
00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.430
potuz: Compatible with your head.

57
00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.129
potuz: And nothing else.

58
00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:36.679
potuz: So this already takes care of multiple bids on multiple branches, and multiple bids on cases where you're reorging.

59
00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:50.189
potuz: I know that there's a subtlety between honest… get proposer head and your head, but again, this… this, I think, is much safer than allowing builders to keep increasing the bid on a bid that will not be selected by proposers.

60
00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:58.930
Justin Traglia: I actually agree, and POTUS.

61
00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.940
Justin Traglia: Er. Sorry, your hand is still up.

62
00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:08.090
potuz: Oh, I'm sorry, it's this damn client, I need to lower it myself.

63
00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.799
Justin Traglia: No worries.

64
00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.319
Justin Traglia: I mean, what you said actually makes sense to me.

65
00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.890
Justin Traglia: But they should just keep track of builds, or sorry, bids.

66
00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.090
Justin Traglia: That work for their head.

67
00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.580
